From 449d86e91550b5211881708cbb2b0ef9cb780daa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Fran=C3=A7ois=20Roux?= <info@humanlearning.ch>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 14:30:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] wifi: ath12k: Do not count a vdev restart as a newly
 started vdev
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ath12k_mac_vdev_start_restart() increments ar->num_started_vdevs on every
call, including the restart issued by a channel switch (CSA). With a single
vdev the counter reaches 2 after a CSA while the firmware keeps sending one
VDEV_STAT event, so num_vdev_recvd never equals num_started_vdevs,
fw_stats_done never completes, and every later stats request ends with
"time out while waiting for fw stats done".

Observed on a Surface Pro 12in (WCN7850) on 2026-09-12: eight seconds after
"CTRL-EVENT-CHANNEL-SWITCH freq=5180 ch_width=160 MHz" the message repeated
3087 times over five hours and the link was unusable until a reboot.

Root cause and fix are Baochen Qiang's, from the linux-wireless thread
"ath12k: WCN7850 fw stats permanently wedge after CSA" (July 2026). Not yet
in mainline as of 7.3-rc3; carried here until it lands.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
Signed-off-by: François Roux <info@humanlearning.ch>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
index af354bef5c0d..ef0f87a579b2 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mac.c
@@ -11392,7 +11392,15 @@ ath12k_mac_vdev_start_restart(struct ath12k_link_vif *arvif,
 						   &arvif->reg_tpc_info);
 	}
 
-	ar->num_started_vdevs++;
+	/*
+	 * SP12: a restart (channel switch, CSA) must not count as a new
+	 * started vdev, or fw_stats_done never completes afterwards and
+	 * every stats request times out ("time out while waiting for fw
+	 * stats done"). Root cause and fix from Baochen Qiang, linux-wireless,
+	 * July 2026 ("ath12k: WCN7850 fw stats permanently wedge after CSA").
+	 */
+	if (!restart)
+		ar->num_started_vdevs++;
 	ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_MAC,  "vdev %pM started, vdev_id %d\n",
 		   ahvif->vif->addr, arvif->vdev_id);
 
-- 
